There are 9 cells of 8, 4 of 7 and 1 of 6, matching the interior sizes. Nothing outside a frame changes.\n\nThere is no obvious formula linking size to colour, so I use a lookup table keyed on interior area: `{9: 8, 4: 7, 1: 6}`.\n\n**Test input:** it has a 5×5 frame (interior becomes 8), a 4×4 frame (interior becomes 7) and a 3×3 frame (centre becomes 6). All three sizes appear in the training pairs, so the table covers every case.\n\n**Construction:**\n1. Start from a copy of the input.\n2. For each frame, fill the background cells inside its bounding box (the box shrunk by one cell on each side) with the colour for that interior area.\n3. Emit the canvas after each frame is filled.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    table = {9: 8, 4: 7, 1: 6}\n    for o in objects(g, bg=bg):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        if y1 - y0 < 2 or x1 - x0 < 2:\n            continue\n        inner = out[y0+1:y1, x0+1:x1]\n        mask = g[y0+1:y1, x0+1:x1] == bg\n        area = int(mask.sum())\n        if area in table:\n            inner[mask] = table[area]\n            emit(out, f\"Filled the {area}-cell interior of the frame at {o['box']} with colour {table[area]}.\")\n    emit(out, \"All frames filled according to interior size.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The fill colour depends only on how big the interior is:"},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **3×3 interior** (5×5 frame, 16 cells): filled with 8."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- **2×2 interior** (4×4 frame, 12 cells): filled with 7."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Every changed cell is a 0 strictly inside a frame's bounding box."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"For each frame, fill the background cells inside its bounding box (the box shrunk by one cell on each side) with the colour for that interior area."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"c68a288c53f8bed8fbe0b0caa2ab0a2a9094ab3a38319bc6439b16ff54e09f24","task_sha256":"fde2f162b775b2e4fc3484edf18cee08d886c71c864e236d821f36fefcb5c89f","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
